Z||000000||GTFiero1||11-09-2001||04:02 AM||||i may get an 88 coupe. its not a definate but a possibility but it needs a new clutch. its the tech 4 with the 5-speed. how much would a new clutch cost and about how much to get one installed<P>------------------<BR>Adam J. B.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Rare87GT||11-09-2001||10:30 AM||||Clutch is probably around $100-$150.  To get it installed I'm not sure.  When we called the dealership where I got my car, they said about $1800, and I bought the car for only $1500.  I would definitely say getting it installed by someone else is going to cost you a lot of money.<P>------------------<BR>1987 GT *5 Speed*<BR>(Canadian Car)<BR>2.8L Mods--No Cat, K&N||||reg||1
Z||000002||kempo||11-09-2001||11:55 AM||||Most garages will charge you around the $1000 mark.  I know a guy who just paid $820 for his to be done at the shop, labor alone.  Prices vary from place to place.  I'd definitely do it myself, but in reality, if you don't have the tools and/or know-how to do it yourself, have a few knowledgeable friends do it over a case or two.  It's always easier to dish out $50 or even $100 than $1000.  Now the clutch itself should cost about $150.  Either way, best of luck!<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.admist.net/gtsmall.jpg">    <BR>0-60 6.9 seconds||||reg||1
Z||000003||Brandon86SE||11-09-2001||10:37 PM||||I paid about $1000 Canadian for my clutch job.  They also replaced a leaky oilpan at the same time.  Most of that was labour, about $250 for the clutch/oil pan.  It wasn't cheap, but that was a year ago, and I didn't know a thing about being a backyard mechanic yet.<P>Brandon<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Field_Front_(sig)_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
